<title>USA: Healthsource 1997 Q1 shr $0.11 vs $0.22.</title>
<headline>Healthsource 1997 Q1 shr $0.11 vs $0.22.</headline>
<dateline>HOOKSETT, N.H. 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>				 Three months ended March 31,</p>
<p>				   1997		  1996</p>
<p>Total operating</p>
<p>  revenue		   $ 476,761	   $ 419,092</p>
<p>Total operating</p>
<p>  expenses		    467,551	     399,196</p>
<p> Operating income	     9,210		19,896</p>
<p>Interest and other</p>
<p>  income, net		   2,317		 4,088</p>
<p>Income before provision</p>
<p>  for income taxes	   11,527		23,984</p>
<p>Provision for income</p>
<p>  taxes			  (4,551)	     (8,422)</p>
<p> Net income		     6,976		15,562</p>
<p>Preferred stock</p>
<p>  dividend			   --		(1,128)</p>
<p>Net income available to</p>
<p>  common shareholders	 6,976		14,434</p>
<p> Net income per share	  0.11		  0.22</p>
<p>Weighted average number</p>
<p>of common and common</p>
<p>equivalent shares</p>
<p>  outstanding		  64,266		65,953</p>
<p>NOTE: Earnings per share for the first quarter of 1997 were $0.13 before the effect of a non-recurring charge of $0.02 per share primarily related to first quarter merger development costs. On February 28, the company announced a definitive agreement  with CIGNA Corp subject to regulatory and other approvals. Full company name is Healthsource Inc.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
